## Round 2

The targeted Red command, rerun before any edit, failed as the Red log names: exit 1, 15 failed
and 2 passed (the two named characterizations).

Implementation. `lib/teacher-loops.ts` holds the rule module (`loopsShow`, `loopPanelsShow`,
`stepTimeMinutes`). `lesson-flow.tsx` renders the recall region at the day opening, the three
loop panels inside the step sections, the clip controls from the signed map, and the step time
`loopMinutes ?? minutes`. Each step section carries `key={step.id}`: React reuses the section
element without the key, so the DOM node that the test harness holds after the walk shows the
last step. The panels use the brand classes (amber `#fcd34d` with brown `#92400e` text, or brown
with white text); no blue class.

Round 2 found one un-satisfiable Red assertion: the test built its own signed map with
`https://signed.example/<file>`, where every drill file holds the `phonemes/daniel/` prefix, and
then asserted `data-clip-url` equals the map value and, on the same value, does not contain
`phonemes/daniel/`. No implementation could pass. Round 2 stopped and requested a Mid Red retry;
Red fixed the test in `d1d500b66` and `0544fb6e4`.

